    "faq": {
      "type": "bella-faq",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Questions",
        "heading": "3D product rendering services, answered",
        "open_first": true
      },
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are 3D product rendering services?",
            "answer": "3D product rendering services create photorealistic images of a product from a 3D model instead of a camera. A 3D artist builds the model from photos, dimensions and spec sheets, applies the real materials, then renders white-background product images, lifestyle scenes and colour variants. Furniture brands, retailers and e-commerce teams use them for product pages, catalogues and marketing campaigns, often in place of traditional product photography."
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the difference between 3D modeling and 3D rendering?",
            "answer": "3D modeling builds the product: the geometry, dimensions and details of a three dimensional digital object. 3D rendering turns that model into images by adding materials, lighting and a camera. You need the model once; after that it can be rendered again in new finishes, rooms and camera angles."
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much do 3D product rendering and 3D modeling cost?",
            "answer": "Bella prices 3D modeling and rendering by quote. The cost depends on how many products you have, how complex each one is, how many colour and material variants you need, and how many white-background or lifestyle images each product needs. Send us your product list and we'll quote the whole project: <a href=\"/pages/contact-us\">contact us for a quote</a>."
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What do you need from me to start a 3D furniture rendering project?",
            "answer": "Product photos, overall dimensions, spec sheets and material swatches, or high-resolution photos of each fabric, leather, wood and metal finish. If you already have technical drawings or CAD files, send them too and we'll tell you how we can use them. A short list of the images you need for each product helps us quote accurately."
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does 3D furniture rendering take?",
            "answer": "Timelines depend on catalogue size and product complexity: a handful of pieces is a different schedule from a full range with dozens of variants. We'll give you a schedule with your quote."
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are your 3D models made with AI?",
            "answer": "No. Every model is built by hand by Bella's own 3D artists in 3ds Max. AI image generators and other AI-enhanced tools can generate a convincing picture of a sofa, but not reliably your sofa: dimensions, seams and finishes drift from the real product, which becomes a problem when a customer compares the delivered piece with the image they bought from."
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you render furniture before it's manufactured?",
            "answer": "3D rendering is widely used to show furniture before it is produced, so marketing can start before the first production run. If a piece is still in development, send the drawings, dimensions and spec sheets you have, and we'll tell you what else we need to model it accurately."
          }
        },
        "q8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you show every colour and fabric option?",
            "answer": "Yes. Colour and material variants are rendered from the same 3D model, so each fabric, leather, wood or metal finish appears in the same lighting and camera angles as the rest of the range."
          }
        },
        "q9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you create lifestyle scenes as well as white-background images?",
            "answer": "Yes. We deliver photoreal renders on a white background and lifestyle renders of your furniture in styled rooms. Our 3D team also maintains Bella's Look Book of Contemporary, Modern Farmhouse, Scandinavian, Coastal, Mid-Century Modern, Traditional and Transitional styles, so a room can be styled in the direction that suits your brand."
          }
        },
        "q10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I get 3D model files for my website, configurator or augmented reality (AR) viewer?",
            "answer": "Ask us about file formats for your website, configurator or AR viewer when you request your quote."
          }
        },
        "q11": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you offer 3D modeling and rendering services in Canada, including Toronto and Vancouver?",
            "answer": "Yes. Bella provides 3D modeling and rendering services across Canada and the US. Furniture brands, retailers and builders looking for 3D product rendering services in Toronto, a 3D product rendering agency in Vancouver or a studio in Montreal work with us online: photos, specs, drafts and revisions all move online."
          }
        },
        "q12": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you offer 3D modeling services for home builders?",
            "answer": "Yes. For home builders we model plans and homes for marketing. See <a href=\"/products/3d-rendering-service-for-architectural-visualization\">3D architectural rendering</a> for exteriors and interiors built from plans, <a href=\"/pages/home-builder-marketing\">home builder marketing</a> for the full builder toolkit, and <a href=\"/pages/virtual-staging-texas\">virtual staging in Texas</a> for model homes and new construction."
          }
        },
        "q13": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you offer 3D architectural modelling services?",
            "answer": "Yes. Architectural visualization is a separate Bella service: our 3D artists model buildings from floor plans, elevations and CAD files and render photoreal exteriors and interiors. See our <a href=\"/pages/3d-rendering-services\">3D rendering services</a>."
          }
        },
        "q14": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What software do 3D product modelers use?",
            "answer": "Bella's artists work in 3ds Max. Across the industry, furniture and product studios also model in tools such as Rhino and Blender and render with physically based rendering engines such as V-Ray and Corona, according to Chaos. You don't need any specialized software to order: send your product information and our team does the modeling."
          }
        },
        "q15": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is 3D rendering cheaper than furniture photography?",
            "answer": "It depends on the range. For a single hero shot of a product you already have, photography can be simpler. For wide ranges, many finishes or products that aren't made yet, rendering removes the samples, shipping, sets and reshoots; IKEA began moving its product images to CGI renders partly to save the cost of building and shipping prototype furniture to be photographed. We'll quote your project so you can compare."
          }
        },
        "q16": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What should I look for in 3D product visualization companies?",
            "answer": "Look for a portfolio with products like yours, artists who model from your real specs rather than generating images with AI, material accuracy that holds up in close-ups, consistency across a whole catalogue, a clear review and revision process, and a written quote and schedule before the project begins."
          }
        }
      },
